WEBVTT

00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:06.780
How does the AI Confidence Academy help
you build confidence with AI?

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:12.680
We begin by giving confidence a practical
meaning. It means knowing how to take part

00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:16.900
in a conversation, how to recognize a
useful response,

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:22.320
and what to do when the response misses
the mark. It also means being

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:26.460
comfortable saying, I need to check that
before I rely on it.

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:30.920
You do not build those abilities by
watching someone else do everything.

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:32.660
You build them by participating,

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:34.980
examining the result,

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:38.080
and trying again with a clearer
understanding.

00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:40.500
Consider an everyday task:

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:45.220
organizing a project you have been putting
off. You describe what you want to

00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:49.260
accomplish, the time you have, and the
limits you need to work within.

00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:51.300
AI gives you a plan.

00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:54.160
Now your judgment comes into the process.

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:56.460
Does the plan fit your circumstances?

00:00:57.340 --> 00:00:59.300
Has it included something you cannot
afford?

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:04.780
Has it assumed you have help that you do
not have? You identify the problem and

00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:05.900
give clearer direction.

00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:11.580
Perhaps you say, I am doing this alone.
Break the first step into something

00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:13.040
I can complete this afternoon.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:15.920
Then you examine the revised plan.

00:01:16.540 --> 00:01:21.260
You are learning to shape the assistance
around your life. The useful skill is

00:01:21.260 --> 00:01:25.440
understanding how to direct the work and
evaluate what comes back.

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:31.040
ACA's guided practice gives you
opportunities to develop that skill.

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:32.520
Across the journeys,

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:35.360
you practice explaining your purpose,

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:40.860
adding relevant context, asking follow-up
questions, and

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:44.520
recognizing when an answer needs
correction or verification.

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:50.220
Reflection helps you see what made the
conversation more useful. Our aim is to

00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:52.960
train humans who can use these tools with
understanding.

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:55.260
Your experience still matters.

00:01:55.960 --> 00:01:59.880
Your decisions still belong to you. A
confident learner can accept useful

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:03.240
assistance and question an answer that has
not earned their trust.

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:06.220
That is why we say, AI assists.

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:12.160
Humans verify. Confidence includes knowing
the limits of the assistance and following

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:13.780
through on the checks that matter.

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:19.300
As you practice, notice the small changes.
You can explain what you need

00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:22.100
more clearly. You can identify what is
missing.

00:02:22.840 --> 00:02:26.340
You know how to ask for a correction and
when to consult another source.

00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:30.000
Those are abilities you can carry into the
next task.

00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:33.700
Thank you for joining us. Come begin with
ACA,

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:39.560
and give yourself the opportunity to build
confidence through practice.

